16. An offence u/s 498A thus, has following essential ingredients:
(a) that the victim was a married lady (she may also be a widow);
(b) that she has been subjected to cruelty by her husband or the relatives of husband;
(c) that such cruelty consisted of either (1) harassment of the woman with a view to coerce her for meeting a demand of dowry or (2) a willful conduct by the husband or the relative of the husband of such a nature as is likely to lead the lady to commit suicide or to cause grave injury to her life, limb or health;
(d) that such injury aforesaid may be mental or physical;
17. Section 406 IPC provides punishment for the offence of criminal breach of trust defined under Sec. 405 IPC.
